Multi-Agent Memory public-reference startup packet

Purpose:
- Cold-start packet for agents entering the public Multi-Agent Memory reference repository and its separately governed MemoryEndpoints.com integration boundary.

Verification status: active operational memory; verify with the `.uai` audit before relying on it.
Memory scope: startup order, product target, and active memory boundary.
Public-safe status: safe for source control; contains no credential values.
Update route: update this local file for startup-order changes; submit public-safe durable summaries to https://memoryendpoints.com/api/matm/memory-events/submit when authenticated.
Source of truth: `.uai/totem.uai`, repository files, and verified reports under `docs/reports`.
Next action for agents: follow the read order below before acting.
Must not expose: raw API keys, bearer tokens, FTP credentials, database passwords, private keys, private handoff payloads, or raw one-time keys.

Bootstrap:
- This file is the cold-start index for the local `.uai` memory folder.
- After loading this file, read `.uai/memory-maintenance.uai` first, then identity, world context, and the Totem/Taboo/Talisman anchors before any hosted MATM assumption.
- Every active `.uai` memory file must be represented in the read order or the memory setup is incomplete.
- Do not use README files, bucket-local guidance, status files, or index files as memory-package substitutes.

Read order:
1. .uai/startup-packet.uai
2. .uai/memory-maintenance.uai
3. .uai/identity.uai
4. .uai/world-context.uai
5. .uai/totem.uai
6. .uai/taboo.uai
7. .uai/talisman.uai
8. .uai/system-profile.uai
9. .uai/receiver-brief.uai
10. .uai/index.uai
11. .uai/context.uai
12. .uai/constraints.uai
13. .uai/overview.uai
14. .uai/stack.uai
15. .uai/architecture.uai
16. .uai/coding-standards.uai
17. .uai/operations.uai
18. .uai/test-plan.uai
19. .uai/decisions.uai
20. .uai/risk-register.uai
21. .uai/owners.uai
22. .uai/agent-instructions.uai
23. .uai/agents/memoryendpoints-frontend-agent.uai
24. .uai/agents/memoryendpoints-backend-agent.uai
25. .uai/style.uai
26. .uai/memory.uai
27. .uai/file-handoff.uai
28. .uai/intake-outcome-ledger.uai
29. .uai/handoff-brief.uai
30. .uai/long-term-memory.uai
31. .uai/long-term-pointer-ledger.uai
32. .uai/next-actions.uai
33. .uai/next-recursive-prompt.uai
34. .uai/open-questions.uai
35. .uai/progress.uai

After item 35, read root `workspace.uai` as the public-safe cross-product checkpoint. It is outside this governed manifest and never substitutes for a manifest member.

Target:
Build and verify this checkout as the free single-organization private-intranet Multi-Agent Memory MATM reference, with MultiAgentMemory.com as its public GitHub companion documentation site. Treat MemoryEndpoints.com as a separately governed hosted/commercial integration boundary whose private source and deployment are not present here.

Current boundary:
Use the full `.uai` suite as active startup memory. Every `.uai/*.uai` file in the read order is active memory. Read `.uai/totem.uai` as the invariant: local `.uai` stays active always. Use MemoryEndpoints.com as an external mid-to-long-term MATM endpoint only when reachable, authenticated, and accepted by its owning boundary; never infer its private source or deployment authority from this checkout. Use MultiAgentMemory.com for public documentation and GitHub-facing explanation after its own exact release gates pass.
